-- title:
--   Invertibility of a relative divisor supported in a smooth open
-- statement:
--   Let $f\colon\mathcal C\to S$ be a separated morphism of schemes and let $U\subseteq\mathcal C$ be an open subscheme such that the inclusion $U\hookrightarrow\mathcal C$ followed by $f$ is smooth of relative dimension $1$. Let $r$ be a natural number, let $T$ be a scheme and $g\colon T\to S$ a morphism, and let $D$ be a relative effective Cartier divisor of degree $r$ for $f$ over $g$ in the project's sense: a datum consisting of an ideal sheaf $D.I$ on the fibre product $\mathcal C\times_S T$ whose associated closed subscheme, mapped by its closed immersion followed by the second projection to $T$, is finite, flat and locally of finite presentation over $T$ and has rank exactly $r$ at every point $t$ of $T$. Assume $D$ is supported in $U$, that is, the support of $D.I$, as a subset of $\mathcal C\times_S T$, is contained in the open subset obtained by pulling $U$ back along the first projection. Then $D.I$ is invertible in the sense used here: every point $x$ of $\mathcal C\times_S T$ lies in the basic open set $D(a)$ of some section $a$ over some affine open, and on the affine basic open set determined by $a$ the ideal of $D.I$ is generated by a single non-zerodivisor.
--
--   This is the local principality (Cartier property) of the ideal sheaf of a relative effective divisor, in the form needed when the ambient curve $\mathcal C\to S$ is smooth of relative dimension one only on an open subscheme containing the support of the divisor, rather than everywhere. It is the invertibility input used throughout the subsequent theory of relative divisors on such curves, for instance in the identification of $D.I$ with the ideal of a zero scheme and in the comparison of pullbacks of the associated modules.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_RelEffCartierDiv_isInvertible_I_of_supportedIn.lean

